requirements:
Specifies the number of bags to be selected at random from the lot for drawing increments:
a) For lots of 10 to 100 bags: Sample at least 10 bags;
b) For lots of more than 100 bags: Sample at least 10% of the total bags.

Establishes a standardized framework to audit active rodent presence through physical indicators, including:
a) Fecal pellet count, size, shape, and freshness;
b) Footprint tracking using fine talc dust or tracking patches;
c) Active burrow counting and identification of runway paths; and
d) Structural gnaw marks on wood, bags, or doors.

Specifies the number of cartons to be selected at random based on the lot size:
a) Up to 24 cartons: 2 cartons;
b) 25 to 50 cartons: 8 cartons;
c) 51 to 100 cartons: 10 cartons;
d) 101 to 250 cartons: 12 cartons;
e) 251 to 500 cartons: 14 cartons;
f) 501 to 1 000 cartons: 18 cartons;
g) 1 001 and above: 24 cartons.

Specifies the number of containers to be selected at random based on container count in the lot:
a) Up to 8 containers: 2 containers;
b) 9 to 25 containers: 3 containers;
b) 26 to 50 containers: 5 containers;
c) 51 to 100 containers: 7 containers;
d) 101 to 150 containers: 8 containers;
e) 151 to 300 containers: 9 containers;
f) 301 and above: 10 containers.

Specifies the number of bundles, bags, or packages to be selected at random based on lot size:
a) Up to 8 packages: 2 packages;
b) 9 to 25 packages: 3 packages;
c) 26 to 50 packages: 4 packages;
d) 51 to 100 packages: 5 packages;
e) 101 to 120 packages: 6 packages;
f) 121 and above: 7 packages.

Specifies the number of containers to be selected at random from the lot:
a) Up to 25 containers: 2 containers;
b) 26 to 50 containers: 8 containers;
c) 51 to 100 containers: 13 containers;
d) 101 and above: 20 containers.

Requires picking up fish at random from different parts of selected containers:
a) Large fish (> 2.5 kg): Select at least 2 fish, cut and quarter to obtain a composite sample of approximately 120 g;
b) Medium/Small fish (< 2.5 kg): Select at least 5 fish to construct a representative sample.

Establishes specific minimum, optimum, and maximum temperature and relative humidity parameters governing the population multiplication rates of stored grain pests to guide aeration and temperature controls:
a) Australian spider beetle (Ptinus tectus): Min Temp 10°C, Min RH 50%, Opt Temp 23-25°C, Opt RH 70%, Multiplication: 4x/month;
b) Lesser grain borer (Rhizopertha dominica): Min Temp 23°C, Min RH 30%, Opt Temp 32-35°C, Opt RH 50%, Multiplication: 20x/month;
c) Grain weevil (Sitophilus granarius): Min Temp 15°C, Min RH 50%, Opt Temp 26-30°C, Opt RH 70%, Multiplication: 15x/month;
d) Rice weevil (Sitophilus oryzae): Min Temp 17°C, Min RH 60%, Opt Temp 27-31°C, Opt RH 70%, Multiplication: 25x/month.
